1
00:00:01,585 --> 00:00:03,128
YOU KNOW WHAT?
IT SEEMS LIKE
ALL OF A SUDDEN

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:04,505
SO MUCH IS HAPPENING.

3
00:00:04,546 --> 00:00:07,215
I KNOW. ROSS IS
GETTING MARRIED...

4
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:10,594
PHOEBE'S... MAKING PEOPLE.

5
00:00:10,636 --> 00:00:12,011
EVERYBODY'S DOING STUFF.

6
00:00:12,053 --> 00:00:13,263
AND WE JUST SIT HERE.

7
00:00:13,305 --> 00:00:14,640
IF I DIED, THE ONLY WAY

8
00:00:14,682 --> 00:00:16,558
PEOPLE WOULD EVEN KNOW
THAT I WAS HERE

9
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,686
WOULD BE BY THE ASS PRINT
ON THIS CHAIR.

10
00:00:20,061 --> 00:00:22,063
LOOK, WE HAVE
TO DO SOMETHING, OKAY?

11
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:23,064
SOMETHING HUGE.

12
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:24,107
( snaps finger )

13
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:25,985
WE COULD CLIMB MT. EVEREST.

14
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:29,780
NO. NOT SOMETHING STUPID--
SOMETHING HUGE.

15
00:00:29,822 --> 00:00:31,699
NO, NO, I SAW AN AD
FOR THIS VIDEO.

16
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,534
PEOPLE CLIMB THAT THING
EVERY DAY.

17
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:35,243
WE COULD TOTALLY DO THAT.

18
00:00:35,285 --> 00:00:38,789
WHY NOT? I MEAN, IT'S JUST...
IT'S JUST CLIMBING.

19
00:00:38,831 --> 00:00:40,791
IT'S JUST... IT'S JUST STEEP.

20
00:00:40,833 --> 00:00:42,083
YEAH.

21
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:43,669
WE'RE GOING TO EVEREST, OKAY?

22
00:00:43,711 --> 00:00:46,213
IT'D BE NICE TO LEAVE
AN ASS PRINT ON EVEREST.

23
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:48,590
HEY.
HEY.

24
00:00:48,632 --> 00:00:49,800
HEY, WHAT'S UP?

25
00:00:49,842 --> 00:00:50,801
WE'RE GOING TO CLIMB
MT. EVEREST.

26
00:00:50,843 --> 00:00:52,594
YEAH, BABY!
REALLY.

27
00:00:52,636 --> 00:00:54,346
I LOOKED INTO THAT.

28
00:00:54,388 --> 00:00:57,349
YEAH, BUT I MEAN, IT COSTS,
LIKE, $60,000

29
00:00:57,391 --> 00:00:59,184
AND, YOU KNOW, YOU COULD DIE

30
00:00:59,226 --> 00:01:02,563
AND... YOU WOULD DIE.

31
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:06,066
OH... WELL.

32
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:07,693
WE COULD GET
THAT EVEREST VIDEO THOUGH.

33
00:01:07,735 --> 00:01:09,194
YEAH, WE COULD DO THAT

34
00:01:09,236 --> 00:01:11,530
WITHOUT, YOU KNOW,
RISKING OUR LIVES AT ALL.

35
00:01:11,572 --> 00:01:13,448
AND WHILE WE'RE DOWN
AT THE VIDEO STORE

36
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:14,491
YOU KNOW
WHAT ELSE WE COULD RENT?

37
00:01:14,533 --> 00:01:15,492
DIE HARD.

38
00:01:17,036 --> 00:01:18,662
OH, BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?

39
00:01:18,704 --> 00:01:20,121
I JUST REMEMBERED
THAT EVEREST THING

40
00:01:20,163 --> 00:01:22,165
IS ONLY AVAILABLE
THROUGH MAIL ORDER.

41
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:23,918
OH, WELL.

42
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:26,169
SO YOU GUYS WILL STAY HERE
AND HANG OUT WITH ME?

43
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:29,172
YEAH.
YEAH.

44
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:30,841
BUT I'LL TELL YOU SOMETHING.

45
00:01:30,883 --> 00:01:33,761
ONE OF THESE DAYS,
WE'RE GOING TO GET OFF OUR BUTTS

46
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:35,136
AND RENT DIE HARD AGAIN.

47
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:36,972
YEAH, WE ARE!

48
00:01:42,101 --> 00:01:47,066
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

49
00:01:47,106 --> 00:01:49,359
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

50
00:01:49,401 --> 00:01:51,612
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

51
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:56,617
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

52
00:01:56,658 --> 00:01:58,243
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

53
00:01:58,285 --> 00:02:02,163
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

54
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:05,709
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

55
00:02:05,751 --> 00:02:08,087
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

56
00:02:08,127 --> 00:02:10,756
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

57
00:02:10,798 --> 00:02:12,883
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

58
00:02:12,925 --> 00:02:15,677
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

59
00:02:15,719 --> 00:02:20,682
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

60
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:27,481
SO WHAT DID WE DECIDE?

61
00:02:27,522 --> 00:02:29,858
DOES YOUR UNCLE NATHAN
GET AN INVITE OR NOT?

62
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:32,111
OH, GOD, NOBODY
LIKES HIM.

63
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,862
AND HE'S SO CHEAP.

64
00:02:33,904 --> 00:02:36,073
I MEAN, HE'D NEVER FLY TO
LONDON IN A MILLION YEARS.

65
00:02:36,115 --> 00:02:37,699
YEAH, INVITE HIM.

66
00:02:37,741 --> 00:02:42,370
HEY, DID I DO THESE
NEAT ENOUGH?

67
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:44,665
YEAH. THEY'RE FINE.
YEAH?

68
00:02:44,706 --> 00:02:45,916
IF ANYONE ASKS

69
00:02:45,958 --> 00:02:47,542
WE'LL SAY THAT BEN
ADDRESSED THEM.

70
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:48,627
( chuckles )

71
00:02:48,669 --> 00:02:51,046
OH. SO YOU INVITED
RACHEL, THEN?

72
00:02:51,088 --> 00:02:52,798
SURE. WHY NOT?

73
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:53,799
REALLY?

74
00:02:53,841 --> 00:02:55,174
YEAH.

75
00:02:55,216 --> 00:02:57,176
WELL, DON'T THINK
I'D BE COMFORTABLE

76
00:02:57,218 --> 00:02:59,178
HAVING ANY OF
MY OLD LOVERS THERE.

77
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,597
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.

78
00:03:00,639 --> 00:03:02,850
DO YOU THINK MAYBE WE
SHOULDN'T INVITE HER?

79
00:03:02,891 --> 00:03:04,101
OH, NO, NO, ROSS.

80
00:03:04,143 --> 00:03:06,061
YOU KNOW I ABSOLUTELY
ADORE RACHEL.

81
00:03:06,103 --> 00:03:07,521
IT'S JUST THAT...

82
00:03:07,562 --> 00:03:09,815
WELL, I THOUGHT IT MIGHT BE
A BIT AWKWARD FOR YOU.

83
00:03:09,857 --> 00:03:12,526
BUT IT'S ABSOLUTELY
YOUR DECISION.

84
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:15,737
MORE TEA?
YEAH, SURE.

85
00:03:15,779 --> 00:03:16,905
EARL GREY?

86
00:03:16,947 --> 00:03:18,239
HUH? FINE.

87
00:03:18,281 --> 00:03:20,075
INVITE WHOEVER YOU WANT.

88
00:03:24,830 --> 00:03:26,790
I DON'T WANT TO
BE SINGLE, OKAY?

89
00:03:26,832 --> 00:03:28,416
I JUST, I JUST,
I JUST WANT

90
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:30,418
TO BE MARRIED AGAIN.

91
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:38,593
AND I JUST WANT
A MILLION DOLLARS!

92
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:39,594
RACHEL?

93
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:42,014
OH, GOD, MONICA, HI.

94
00:03:42,056 --> 00:03:43,431
THANK GOD.

95
00:03:45,184 --> 00:03:46,685
Monica:
OKAY, EVERYBODY...

96
00:03:46,727 --> 00:03:48,979
THIS IS RACHEL,
ANOTHER LINCOLN
HIGH SURVIVOR.

97
00:03:49,021 --> 00:03:50,397
THIS IS EVERYBODY.
THIS IS CHANDLER

98
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:51,690
AND PHOEBE

99
00:03:51,732 --> 00:03:53,067
AND JOEY AND...

100
00:03:53,108 --> 00:03:55,110
YOU REMEMBER
MY BROTHER ROSS?
SURE!

101
00:03:55,152 --> 00:03:56,528
HEY.
HI. OH!

102
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:57,529
OH, GOD!

103
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:00,490
YOU KNOW, YOU PROBABLY
DIDN'T KNOW THIS

104
00:04:00,532 --> 00:04:03,326
BUT BACK IN HIGH SCHOOL,
I HAD A, UM...

105
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:04,703
MAJOR CRUSH ON YOU.

106
00:04:04,745 --> 00:04:06,121
I KNEW.

107
00:04:06,163 --> 00:04:07,288
YOU DID? OH.

108
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:08,540
( chuckles )

109
00:04:08,582 --> 00:04:10,417
I ALWAYS FIGURED
YOU JUST THOUGHT

110
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:12,502
I WAS MONICA'S
GEEKY OLDER BROTHER.

111
00:04:12,544 --> 00:04:13,837
I DID.

112
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:15,338
OH!

113
00:04:16,464 --> 00:04:17,841
LISTEN, DO YOU THINK...

114
00:04:17,883 --> 00:04:21,053
I TRY NOT TO LET
MY INTENSE VULNERABILITY

115
00:04:21,095 --> 00:04:22,596
BECOME ANY KIND
OF A FACTOR HERE.

116
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:25,682
BUT DO YOU THINK
IT WOULD BE OKAY

117
00:04:25,724 --> 00:04:27,475
IF I ASKED YOU OUT
SOMETIME, MAYBE?

118
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:29,728
YEAH.

119
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:31,772
MAYBE.

120
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:33,857
OKAY.

121
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:36,651
OKAY, MAYBE I WILL.

122
00:04:38,028 --> 00:04:40,155
SEE, I SEE, UH...

123
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:42,950
BIG PASSION IN YOUR FUTURE.

124
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:44,993
REALLY?
I DO.

125
00:04:45,035 --> 00:04:47,162
OH, ROSS,
YOU'RE SO GREAT.

126
00:04:47,204 --> 00:04:48,663
OH...

127
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:56,130
AH...

128
00:04:57,631 --> 00:05:00,467
IT'S NEVER GOING
TO HAPPEN.

129
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:05,764
YEAH, I'VE A QUESTION.

130
00:05:05,806 --> 00:05:08,683
LOOK, UH, ACTUALLY,
NOT SO MUCH A QUESTION

131
00:05:08,725 --> 00:05:10,811
AS MORE OF A GENERAL
WONDERING... 

132
00:05:12,146 --> 00:05:14,022
...MENT.

133
00:05:14,064 --> 00:05:15,065
OKAY?

134
00:05:15,107 --> 00:05:16,608
OKAY.

135
00:05:16,650 --> 00:05:18,610
UM, WELL, FOR A WHILE NOW,

136
00:05:18,652 --> 00:05:22,447
I'VE BEEN WANTING TO, UM...

137
00:05:22,489 --> 00:05:24,532
OH...
YES, YES.

138
00:05:24,574 --> 00:05:25,617
THAT'S-THAT'S RIGHT.
LOOK AT

139
00:05:25,659 --> 00:05:26,994
THAT LITTLE KITTY!

140
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:28,328
WHAT?

141
00:05:28,369 --> 00:05:30,371
THAT LITTLE KITTY!
( screaming )

142
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:33,541
♪ TOP OF THE WORLD LOOKIN' ♪

143
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:35,294
♪ DOWN ON CREATION ♪

144
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:37,879
♪ AND THE ONLY EXPLANATION ♪

145
00:05:37,921 --> 00:05:40,882
♪ I CAN FIND... ♪

146
00:05:40,924 --> 00:05:43,051
LISTEN, IF YOU
WANT THIS CART

147
00:05:43,093 --> 00:05:46,054
YOU'RE GOING TO HAVE
TO TAKE ME WITH IT!

148
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:50,600
YES!

149
00:05:50,642 --> 00:05:51,601
DID YOU SEE THAT!?

150
00:05:51,643 --> 00:05:53,020
YOU WERE INCREDIBLE!

151
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:56,106
A BRAND-NEW WOMAN,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

152
00:05:56,148 --> 00:05:57,565
I COULD NOT HAVE
DONE THIS WITHOUT YOU.

153
00:05:57,607 --> 00:05:58,566
NO, IT'S JUST...

154
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:06,449
OKAY, UM, UH...

155
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:08,702
MORE CLOTHES
IN THE DRYER?

156
00:06:08,743 --> 00:06:09,744
OH!

157
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:11,079
OH!

158
00:06:11,121 --> 00:06:12,664
I'M FINE. I'M FINE.

159
00:06:12,706 --> 00:06:13,832
YOU HAVE NO RIGHT
TO TELL ME

160
00:06:13,874 --> 00:06:15,583
YOU EVER HAD
FEELINGS FOR ME.

161
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:16,751
WHAT?

162
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:17,961
I WAS DOING GREAT
WITH JULIE

163
00:06:18,003 --> 00:06:19,546
BEFORE I FOUND OUT
ABOUT YOU.

164
00:06:19,587 --> 00:06:21,798
I WAS DOING GREAT
BEFORE I FOUND OUT ABOUT YOU.

165
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:24,301
YOU THINK IT'S EASY FOR ME
TO SEE YOU WITH JULIE?

166
00:06:24,343 --> 00:06:27,304
THE POINT IS, I...
I DON'T NEED THIS RIGHT NOW.

167
00:06:27,346 --> 00:06:29,223
OKAY? IT'S-IT'S
TOO LATE.

168
00:06:29,264 --> 00:06:31,016
I'M SOMEBODY ELSE;
I'M HAPPY.

169
00:06:31,058 --> 00:06:32,391
THIS SHIP HAS SAILED.

170
00:06:32,433 --> 00:06:33,727
FINE. GO AND DO THAT.

171
00:06:33,768 --> 00:06:35,062
FINE. FINE.

172
00:06:35,103 --> 00:06:36,604
I DON'T NEED YOUR STUPID SHIP!

173
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:37,605
GOOD.

174
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:42,236
OH!

175
00:06:42,277 --> 00:06:43,737
( exasperated sigh )

176
00:06:45,655 --> 00:06:48,783
( sobbing )

177
00:07:25,987 --> 00:07:27,406
ROSS, DO YOU REALIZE
THIS IS

178
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:29,116
THE FIRST TIME IN MY LIFE
I'M DOING SOMETHING

179
00:07:29,157 --> 00:07:31,410
I ACTUALLY CARE ABOUT?
THIS IS THE FIRST
TIME IN MY LIFE

180
00:07:31,450 --> 00:07:33,578
I'M DOING SOMETHING
I'M ACTUALLY GOOD AT?

181
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:35,247
IF YOU DON'T GET THAT...

182
00:07:35,289 --> 00:07:37,416
I GET THAT BIG TIME,
AND I'M HAPPY FOR YOU

183
00:07:37,457 --> 00:07:39,334
BUT I'M TIRED
OF HAVING A RELATIONSHIP

184
00:07:39,376 --> 00:07:40,668
WITH YOUR
ANSWERING MACHINE.

185
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:42,129
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO DO ANYMORE.

186
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:43,380
LOOK, NEITHER DO I!

187
00:07:43,422 --> 00:07:45,006
IS THIS ABOUT MARK?

188
00:07:45,048 --> 00:07:46,758
( exasperated sigh )

189
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:47,759
OH, MY GOD!

190
00:07:47,801 --> 00:07:48,760
OKAY, IT'S NOT.

191
00:07:48,802 --> 00:07:49,761
OH, MY GOD!

192
00:07:49,803 --> 00:07:51,554
I CANNOT KEEP HAVING

193
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:53,765
THIS SAME FIGHT
OVER AND OVER AGAIN, ROSS.

194
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:56,684
NO, YOU'RE MAKING THIS TOO HARD!

195
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:57,852
I'M MAKING THIS TOO HARD?

196
00:07:57,894 --> 00:07:59,062
WHAT DO YOU WANT ME TO DO?

197
00:07:59,104 --> 00:08:00,605
I DON'T KNOW!
I DON'T KNOW!

198
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:03,191
LOOK, MAYBE WE SHOULD
JUST TAKE A BREAK.

199
00:08:03,233 --> 00:08:05,193
YOU'RE RIGHT.
LET'S TAKE A BREAK.

200
00:08:05,235 --> 00:08:06,653
LET'S COOL OFF, OKAY?

201
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:09,114
LET'S GET SOME FROZEN YOGURT
OR SOMETHING.

202
00:08:09,156 --> 00:08:10,240
NO...

203
00:08:10,282 --> 00:08:11,825
( sighs )

204
00:08:11,866 --> 00:08:13,701
A BREAK FROM US.

205
00:08:17,872 --> 00:08:19,291
DO I KNOW WHY
WE'RE RUSHING?

206
00:08:19,333 --> 00:08:20,792
YEAH. YOU KNOW
THE GIRLFRIEND

207
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:22,294
I TOLD YOU ABOUT
LAST NIGHT?

208
00:08:22,336 --> 00:08:23,670
WELL, IT TURNS OUT

209
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:25,797
THAT SHE WANTS TO GET BACK
TOGETHER WITH ME...

210
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:27,090
OH, I FOUND IT!

211
00:08:27,132 --> 00:08:29,009
THAT'S SO GREAT
FOR YOU GUYS!

212
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,093
YEAH.

213
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:31,928
GOOD LUCK
WITH YOUR GIRLFRIEND.

214
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:32,929
OH, THANK YOU.

215
00:08:32,971 --> 00:08:34,055
I... HEY!

216
00:08:34,097 --> 00:08:35,640
( giggling )

217
00:08:37,058 --> 00:08:38,810
RACHEL!

218
00:08:38,852 --> 00:08:40,520
HI!

219
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:43,023
OH... YOU GOT
MY MESSAGE, HUH?

220
00:08:43,064 --> 00:08:45,275
YEAH. OH, YOU
ARE RIGHT ON TIME!

221
00:08:45,317 --> 00:08:47,944
SO, WHAT DO YOU SAY--
CAN I BE YOUR GIRLFRIEND AGAIN?

222
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:49,654
YES, YOU CAN,
VERY MUCH.

223
00:08:49,696 --> 00:08:52,073
AH...!

224
00:08:53,367 --> 00:08:55,327
I WANT YOU TO LEAVE.
JUST GET OUT!

225
00:08:55,369 --> 00:08:57,454
I WANT TO STAY.
I WANT TO TALK ABOUT THIS.

226
00:08:57,496 --> 00:08:59,873
ALL RIGHT. HOW WAS SHE?

227
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:01,291
UH-OH.

228
00:09:04,211 --> 00:09:05,879
WH-WHAT?

229
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,005
WAS SHE GOOD?

230
00:09:07,047 --> 00:09:08,215
DON'T ANSWER THAT.

231
00:09:10,342 --> 00:09:12,177
COME ON, ROSS, YOU SAID YOU
WANTED TO TALK TO TALK ABOUT IT.

232
00:09:12,219 --> 00:09:14,012
LET'S TALK ABOUT IT.
HOW WAS SHE?

233
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:16,306
SHE WAS...

234
00:09:16,348 --> 00:09:17,307
AWFUL.

235
00:09:17,349 --> 00:09:18,558
HORRIBLE.
NOT GOOD.

236
00:09:18,599 --> 00:09:20,185
NOTHING
COMPARED TO YOU.

237
00:09:20,227 --> 00:09:22,062
SHE WAS DIFFERENT.

238
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:23,646
UH-OH!
OOH!

239
00:09:25,232 --> 00:09:26,816
GOOD DIFFERENT?

240
00:09:26,858 --> 00:09:29,110
NOBODY LIKES CHANGE.

241
00:09:29,152 --> 00:09:30,945
I...

242
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:32,280
JUST STOP THAT!

243
00:09:32,322 --> 00:09:33,781
WHAT? OKAY! OKAY!

244
00:09:33,823 --> 00:09:36,159
THE WAY YOU OWNED UP
TO EVERYTHING

245
00:09:36,201 --> 00:09:40,579
IT JUST SHOWED ME HOW MUCH
YOU'VE GROWN, YOU KNOW?

246
00:09:40,621 --> 00:09:44,042
I MEAN, MY MOM NEVER
THOUGHT THIS WOULD WORK OUT.

247
00:09:44,084 --> 00:09:45,752
( mirthless chuckle )

248
00:09:45,793 --> 00:09:49,089
SHE WAS ALL,
"ONCE A CHEATER,
ALWAYS A CHEATER."

249
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:51,508
MM-HMM.

250
00:09:51,550 --> 00:09:53,510
OH... I JUST WISH

251
00:09:53,552 --> 00:09:56,054
WE HADN'T LOST
THOSE FOUR MONTHS.

252
00:09:56,096 --> 00:09:58,557
BUT IF TIME IS
WHAT YOU NEEDED

253
00:09:58,598 --> 00:10:01,726
JUST TO GET A LITTLE
PERS-PEC-TIVE...

254
00:10:01,768 --> 00:10:04,020
THAT'S...

255
00:10:04,062 --> 00:10:07,524
( shouting ):
WE WERE ON A BREAK!

256
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:19,619
YOU SEEM TO
REALLY LIKE HER.

257
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:20,703
YEAH, BUT WHAT AM I
GOING TO DO?

258
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:22,456
WE BOTH AGREED
IT WAS GOING TO BE

259
00:10:22,497 --> 00:10:25,792
A TWO-WEEK THING, YOU KNOW--
NO COMMITMENT.

260
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:28,878
ROSS, THAT GIRL JUST SPENT
THE ENTIRE EVENING

261
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:30,589
TALKING TO YOUR FRIENDS,

262
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:34,008
ASKING TO HEAR
STORIES ABOUT YOU,

263
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:36,470
LOOKING THROUGH
MONICA'S PHOTO ALBUMS...

264
00:10:36,511 --> 00:10:37,887
I MEAN,
YOU DON'T DO THAT

265
00:10:37,929 --> 00:10:39,889
IF YOU'RE JUST IN IT
FOR TWO WEEKS.

266
00:10:39,931 --> 00:10:42,142
YOU THINK? HUH.

267
00:10:42,183 --> 00:10:43,935
YOU'VE GOT,
LIKE, 14 HOURS

268
00:10:43,977 --> 00:10:46,313
UNTIL SHE HAS
TO BE AT THE AIRPORT

269
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:49,107
AND YOU'RE SITTING HERE
IN THE HALLWAY WITH A...

270
00:10:49,149 --> 00:10:52,486
28-YEAR-OLD CHEERLEADER
WITH A FAT LIP.

271
00:10:52,527 --> 00:10:55,155
( chuckles )

272
00:10:55,196 --> 00:10:56,990
HEY, YOU'RE RIGHT.

273
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:58,325
YEAH.

274
00:11:04,831 --> 00:11:06,416
( mailbox door closes )

275
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:11,546
OH, THIS IS
SO AMAZING.

276
00:11:11,588 --> 00:11:13,047
I CAN'T BELIEVE

277
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:14,633
MY BROTHER'S GETTING MARRIED
AND IN LONDON.

278
00:11:14,673 --> 00:11:17,469
I MEAN, IT'S SO ROMANTIC.

279
00:11:18,845 --> 00:11:20,472
HEY, PRETTY SMART.

280
00:11:20,514 --> 00:11:21,973
TISSUE PAPER.

281
00:11:22,015 --> 00:11:24,643
YOU'RE AT THE WEDDING,
YOU HAVE TO CRY...

282
00:11:24,683 --> 00:11:29,230
"HANDKERCHIEF?"
"NO. I GOT MY INVITATION."

283
00:11:29,272 --> 00:11:31,149
OH, LOOK!
ISN'T THIS ADORABLE?

284
00:11:31,191 --> 00:11:34,194
ROSS LET BEN ADDRESS MINE.

285
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:35,529
HELLO.

286
00:11:35,570 --> 00:11:37,238
All:
HEY.

287
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:40,450
HEY, DID YOU GET YOUR INVITATION
TO ROSS'S WEDDING?

288
00:11:40,492 --> 00:11:41,784
NO.

289
00:11:41,826 --> 00:11:43,495
WELL, DON'T WORRY, MAN.

290
00:11:43,537 --> 00:11:46,540
I GET TO BRING A GUEST.
WE'LL SHOW HIM.

291
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:48,041
SO JEALOUS YOU'RE ALL GOING.

292
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:49,543
I CAN'T BELIEVE I NEVER KNEW

293
00:11:49,584 --> 00:11:51,752
YOU CAN'T FLY
IN YOUR THIRD TRIMESTER.

294
00:11:51,794 --> 00:11:53,254
I DIDN'T KNOW EITHER.

295
00:11:53,296 --> 00:11:55,382
I KNEW THAT.

296
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:57,050
SO I DIDN'T KNOW THAT

297
00:11:57,091 --> 00:12:00,094
( chuckling ):
BUT YOU SHOULD
SEE YOUR FACES.

298
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:01,221
HI, GUYS. WHAT'S UP?

299
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:02,389
HEY.
HEY.

300
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:04,098
WE'RE HANGING OUT.

301
00:12:08,895 --> 00:12:10,271
WHAT'S THIS?

302
00:12:10,313 --> 00:12:12,273
IS THIS
ROSS'S WEDDING INVITATION?

303
00:12:12,315 --> 00:12:16,277
SEE, MAYBE THAT'S THE ONE
WE SHOULD HAVE ACTUALLY HIDDEN.

304
00:12:16,319 --> 00:12:18,238
OH, NO, NO. GUYS, COME ON.

305
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:19,906
YOU DON'T HAVE
TO DO THAT.

306
00:12:19,947 --> 00:12:21,991
I'M HAPPY FOR HIM.

307
00:12:22,033 --> 00:12:24,827
I AM. I REALLY... I'M... I...

308
00:12:24,869 --> 00:12:26,663
I'LL WORK ON IT.

309
00:12:26,705 --> 00:12:28,498
I'M SORRY, HONEY.

310
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:30,083
MMM.

311
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:33,420
RACHEL, YOU'RE GOING
TO COME THOUGH, AREN'T YOU?

312
00:12:33,461 --> 00:12:34,588
OH, HONEY

313
00:12:34,629 --> 00:12:36,423
I DON'T KNOW. I...

314
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:38,383
THIS ISN'T ONE
OF THOSE, YOU KNOW

315
00:12:38,425 --> 00:12:40,468
"SHE DOESN'T COME,
WE DON'T COME," RIGHT?

316
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:43,012
BECAUSE I ALREADY
BOUGHT MY TICKET...

317
00:12:44,639 --> 00:12:47,766
YOU KNOW WHAT WOULD BE
REAL WEIRD...

318
00:12:47,808 --> 00:12:49,394
IS IF YOU WEREN'T THERE.

319
00:12:49,436 --> 00:12:51,605
JUST SAY YOU'LL THINK
ABOUT IT, OKAY?

320
00:12:51,646 --> 00:12:54,441
NO, I'LL THINK
ABOUT IT. YEAH.

321
00:12:57,151 --> 00:12:58,445
WHO'S THIS FROM?

322
00:12:58,486 --> 00:12:59,487
OH, THAT'S ROSS'S.

323
00:12:59,529 --> 00:13:00,821
OH.

324
00:13:00,863 --> 00:13:02,490
( clears throat )

325
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:06,869
OH, MY GOD.

326
00:13:07,954 --> 00:13:09,748
HE REMEMBERED!

327
00:13:09,788 --> 00:13:11,040
REMEMBERED WHAT?

328
00:13:11,082 --> 00:13:12,417
IT WAS LIKE MONTHS AGO.

329
00:13:12,459 --> 00:13:14,502
WE WERE WALKING BY
THIS ANTIQUE STORE

330
00:13:14,544 --> 00:13:16,296
AND I SAW THIS PIN
IN THE WINDOW

331
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:18,381
AND I TOLD THEM
THAT IT WAS JUST LIKE

332
00:13:18,423 --> 00:13:21,092
ONE MY GRANDMOTHER HAD
WHEN I WAS A LITTLE GIRL.

333
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:24,137
OH, I CAN'T BELIEVE
HE REMEMBERED.

334
00:13:24,178 --> 00:13:25,888
THIS MUST HAVE COST HIM
A FORTUNE.

335
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:27,223
I CAN'T BELIEVE
HE DID THIS.

336
00:13:27,265 --> 00:13:28,433
ROSS? REMEMBER
BACK IN COLLEGE

337
00:13:28,475 --> 00:13:30,351
WHEN HE FELL
IN LOVE WITH CAROL

338
00:13:30,393 --> 00:13:34,105
AND BOUGHT HER THAT
RIDICULOUSLY EXPENSIVE
CRYSTAL DUCK?

339
00:13:34,147 --> 00:13:35,732
WHAT DID YOU
JUST SAY?

340
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:45,450
( mumbling )

341
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:49,996
OH... MY GOD.

342
00:13:50,037 --> 00:13:51,289
Announcer:
Flight 457

343
00:13:51,331 --> 00:13:53,333
from Beijing now arriving.

344
00:13:56,711 --> 00:13:58,588
OH, MY GOD.

345
00:13:58,630 --> 00:14:00,006
ROSS AND I
WERE IN GRAD SCHOOL.

346
00:14:00,047 --> 00:14:01,508
Ross:
WE HAVEN'T SEEN
EACH OTHER

347
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:02,509
SINCE THEN.

348
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,760
WELL, I LAND IN CHINA.

349
00:14:03,802 --> 00:14:05,637
GUESS WHO'S IN CHARGE
OF THE DIG.

350
00:14:05,679 --> 00:14:06,929
JULIE!

351
00:14:08,431 --> 00:14:09,932
JULIE, ISN'T
THAT GREAT?

352
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:11,601
I MEAN, ISN'T THAT JUST

353
00:14:11,643 --> 00:14:14,853
KICK-YOU-IN-THE-CROTCH,
SPIT-ON-YOUR-NECK FANTASTIC?

354
00:14:17,732 --> 00:14:19,858
OH, THAT IS SO SWEET.

355
00:14:21,695 --> 00:14:22,821
NO...

356
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:23,988
( chuckles )

357
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:26,157
NO, OKAY.
NO, YOU HANG UP.

358
00:14:26,199 --> 00:14:27,992
NO, YOU... OKAY.

359
00:14:28,034 --> 00:14:28,993
OKAY.

360
00:14:29,035 --> 00:14:31,496
ONE, TWO, THREE.

361
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:35,542
WELL, YOU DIDN'T
HANG UP EITHER.

362
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:37,877
SHE DIDN'T HANG UP.
SHE DIDN'T HANG UP.

363
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:44,217
OKAY, NO. NO,
YOU HANG UP.

364
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:46,553
YOU, YOU, YOU...

365
00:14:50,348 --> 00:14:52,433
ROSS?

366
00:14:52,475 --> 00:14:54,477
HI. IT'S RACHEL.

367
00:14:54,519 --> 00:14:59,273
I'M JUST CALLING TO SAY
THAT, UM, EVERYTHING'S FINE

368
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:01,735
AND I'M REALLY HAPPY
FOR YOU

369
00:15:01,776 --> 00:15:04,070
AND YOUR CAT.

370
00:15:06,614 --> 00:15:09,909
SO, OBVIOUSLY, I AM OVER YOU.

371
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:13,162
I AM OVER YOU

372
00:15:13,204 --> 00:15:15,456
AND THAT, MY FRIEND,

373
00:15:15,498 --> 00:15:18,334
IS WHAT THEY CALL "CLOSURE."

374
00:15:20,879 --> 00:15:22,921
RACHEL, GOT A MESSAGE FROM YOU.

375
00:15:22,963 --> 00:15:24,173
OH, MY GOD, ROSS, NO.

376
00:15:24,215 --> 00:15:25,258
HANG UP THE PHONE.

377
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:26,342
GIVE ME THE PHONE.

378
00:15:26,384 --> 00:15:28,052
GIVE ME THE
GODDAMNED PHONE!

379
00:15:28,094 --> 00:15:29,387
GIVE ME THE PHONE.

380
00:15:35,351 --> 00:15:37,896
YOU'RE OVER ME?

381
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:39,856
OH, GOD.

382
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:41,190
WHAT, YOU'RE, UH...

383
00:15:41,232 --> 00:15:42,191
OH, GOD.

384
00:15:42,233 --> 00:15:43,443
Y-YOU'RE OVER ME?

385
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:48,448
WHEN WERE YOU...

386
00:15:48,489 --> 00:15:52,410
UNDER ME?

387
00:15:52,452 --> 00:15:53,787
BASICALLY...

388
00:15:53,828 --> 00:15:54,871
( clears throat )

389
00:15:54,913 --> 00:15:58,124
LATELY, I'VE, UH...

390
00:15:58,165 --> 00:16:02,169
I'VE, UH, SORT OF
HAD FEELINGS FOR YOU.

391
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:03,630
OKAY, I NEED TO LIE DOWN.

392
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:06,716
HE BROKE UP
WITH JULIE.

393
00:16:06,758 --> 00:16:08,134
( chuckles )

394
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:10,804
WELL, GO HUG HER,
FOR GOD'S SAKES!

395
00:16:12,555 --> 00:16:13,681
REALLY?

396
00:16:13,723 --> 00:16:16,100
REALLY.

397
00:16:16,142 --> 00:16:18,018
IT'S ALWAYS
BEEN YOU, RACH.

398
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:19,646
OH, GOD.

399
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:28,028
OH...
OH...

400
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:31,031
LISTEN, I'M SORRY,
I HAD TO WORK TONIGHT.

401
00:16:31,073 --> 00:16:33,451
OH, THAT'S OKAY.

402
00:16:33,493 --> 00:16:34,911
YOU WERE WORTH THE WAIT.

403
00:16:34,953 --> 00:16:36,120
OH.

404
00:16:36,162 --> 00:16:39,499
AND I DON'T JUST
MEAN TONIGHT.

405
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:42,794
♪ I NEVER DREAMED ♪

406
00:16:42,836 --> 00:16:45,922
♪ THAT I'D MEET
SOMEBODY LIKE YOU ♪

407
00:16:49,467 --> 00:16:50,927
♪ I NEVER DREAMED ♪

408
00:16:50,969 --> 00:16:52,553
♪ THAT I'D LOVE SOMEBODY... ♪

409
00:16:52,595 --> 00:16:54,054
WHAT... AH...

410
00:16:57,475 --> 00:16:59,936
♪ NO, I... ♪

411
00:16:59,978 --> 00:17:02,396
♪ DON'T WANNA FALL IN LOVE ♪

412
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:05,441
♪ A WICKED GAME WE PLAY... ♪

413
00:17:05,483 --> 00:17:06,860
OH, GOD!

414
00:17:06,901 --> 00:17:09,696
OH, HONEY...

415
00:17:09,737 --> 00:17:11,280
OH, IT'S OKAY.

416
00:17:11,322 --> 00:17:14,868
OH, NO, YOU JUST ROLLED
OVER THE JUICE BOX.

417
00:17:18,078 --> 00:17:19,956
GUNTHER, PLEASE TELL ME

418
00:17:19,998 --> 00:17:21,332
YOU DIDN'T SAY
ANYTHING TO RACHEL

419
00:17:21,374 --> 00:17:23,543
ABOUT ME AND THE GIRL
FROM THE COPY PLACE.

420
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:24,919
I'M SORRY.

421
00:17:24,961 --> 00:17:27,421
WAS I NOT SUPPOSED TO?

422
00:17:34,428 --> 00:17:36,138
YOU'RE THE ONE
WHO ENDED IT, REMEMBER?

423
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,598
YEAH, BECAUSE I WAS MAD AT YOU

424
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:40,351
NOT BECAUSE
I STOPPED LOVING YOU.

425
00:17:40,393 --> 00:17:42,687
YOU STILL LOVE ME?

426
00:17:42,729 --> 00:17:45,314
NO.

427
00:17:45,356 --> 00:17:46,941
WHAT DOES THIS MEAN?

428
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:49,193
WHAT ARE YOU...?
DO YOU WANT TO...

429
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:50,444
GET BACK TOGETHER?

430
00:17:50,486 --> 00:17:52,279
NO... MAYBE.

431
00:17:52,321 --> 00:17:53,781
I DON'T...

432
00:17:53,823 --> 00:17:55,616
I DON'T KNOW.

433
00:17:55,658 --> 00:17:58,452
I JUST... I FEEL...

434
00:18:07,670 --> 00:18:09,296
I CAN'T BELIEVE
I EVEN THOUGHT

435
00:18:09,338 --> 00:18:10,673
OF GETTING BACK TOGETHER
WITH YOU.

436
00:18:10,715 --> 00:18:12,550
WE ARE SO OVER!

437
00:18:12,592 --> 00:18:14,468
( choked up ):
OH... OH... UH...

438
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:16,095
FINE BY ME!

439
00:18:16,136 --> 00:18:18,639
AND HEY, JUST SO YOU KNOW

440
00:18:18,681 --> 00:18:20,182
IT'S NOT THAT COMMON

441
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:22,476
IT DOESN'T HAPPEN
TO EVERY GUY

442
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:24,687
AND IT IS A BIG DEAL!

443
00:18:25,772 --> 00:18:27,899
I KNEW IT!

444
00:18:38,451 --> 00:18:40,119
Rachel's coming out.

445
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:43,289
Doesn't she
look pretty, Jack?

446
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:44,874
OH, MY GOD!

447
00:18:44,916 --> 00:18:47,126
THIS IS US GETTING READY
FOR THE PROM.

448
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:48,294
OH!

449
00:18:48,335 --> 00:18:50,004
WE DON'T HAVE TO WATCH THIS.

450
00:18:50,046 --> 00:18:52,048
YEAH, WE DO.
COME ON! COME ON!

451
00:18:52,090 --> 00:18:53,716
Judy:
Get a shot
of Monica.

452
00:18:53,758 --> 00:18:56,552
Jack:
WAIT. HOW DO YOU
ZOOM OUT?

453
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:58,345
THERE SHE IS.

454
00:18:58,387 --> 00:18:59,388
WHOA!

455
00:18:59,430 --> 00:19:00,556
SHUT UP!

456
00:19:00,598 --> 00:19:02,892
THE CAMERA ADDS TEN POUNDS.

457
00:19:02,934 --> 00:19:05,728
SO, HOW MANY CAMERAS
ARE ACTUALLY ON YOU?

458
00:19:05,770 --> 00:19:08,773
Monica:
Dad, turn it off!

459
00:19:08,815 --> 00:19:10,024
Jack:
IT IS OFF.

460
00:19:10,066 --> 00:19:11,149
IT'S NOT.

461
00:19:11,191 --> 00:19:12,485
Jack:
RIGHT, ROSS?

462
00:19:14,612 --> 00:19:16,489
OH, COME ON.

463
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:18,783
LOOKING GOOD,
MR. KOTTER.

464
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:23,830
I CAN'T GO TO MY OWN PROM
WITHOUT A DATE.

465
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,832
I CAN'T.
IT'S TOO LATE.

466
00:19:25,873 --> 00:19:28,709
IF YOU'RE NOT GOING,
I DON'T WANT TO GO EITHER.

467
00:19:28,751 --> 00:19:30,920
I HAVE
A WONDERFUL IDEA.

468
00:19:30,962 --> 00:19:33,380
YOU SHOULD TAKE RACHEL
TO THE PROM.

469
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:35,382
WE'VE SEEN ENOUGH.
LET'S TURN IT OFF.

470
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:36,884
NO, NO,
I WANT TO SEE.

471
00:19:36,926 --> 00:19:38,511
WELL, I'M NOT GOING
TO WATCH.

472
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:39,971
Jack:
Come on, kid.

473
00:19:40,013 --> 00:19:41,347
LET'S GO.

474
00:19:41,388 --> 00:19:43,057
Judy:
ARE YOU HANDSOME.

475
00:19:43,099 --> 00:19:44,475
Jack:
LET'S SHOW 'EM!

476
00:19:47,061 --> 00:19:48,521
( nervous chuckle )

477
00:19:48,562 --> 00:19:49,689
OKAY, DAD.

478
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,190
RACHEL, READY OR NOT

479
00:19:51,231 --> 00:19:53,526
HERE COMES
YOUR KNIGHT IN SHINING...

480
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:54,861
OH, NO.

481
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:57,030
BYE! DON'T WAIT UP!

482
00:19:57,071 --> 00:19:58,364
OKAY, CHIP!

483
00:19:58,405 --> 00:20:01,325
LET'S GO.

484
00:20:01,367 --> 00:20:02,827
Judy:
OH, DEAR.

485
00:20:02,869 --> 00:20:04,662
JACK, HOW DO I TURN THIS OFF?

486
00:20:06,246 --> 00:20:09,083
I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU DID THAT.

487
00:20:09,125 --> 00:20:11,627
YEAH, WELL...

488
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:31,438
SEE? HE'S HER LOBSTER.

489
00:20:40,531 --> 00:20:41,949
NO!

490
00:20:41,991 --> 00:20:44,118
YOU'RE REALLY NOT GOING?

491
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:46,162
YEAH.

492
00:20:46,204 --> 00:20:48,789
IT'S JUST GOING
TO BE TOO HARD.

493
00:20:48,831 --> 00:20:53,544
YOU KNOW, I MEAN,
IT'S ROSS.

494
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:58,007
HOW CAN I WATCH
HIM GET MARRIED?

495
00:20:58,049 --> 00:20:59,842
YOU KNOW, IT'S JUST,
IT'S FOR THE BEST,
YOU KNOW?

496
00:20:59,884 --> 00:21:01,385
IT IS. IT'S...

497
00:21:01,427 --> 00:21:04,097
PLUS, SOMEBODY'S GOT TO
STAY HERE WITH PHOEBE.

498
00:21:04,138 --> 00:21:07,265
YOU KNOW, SHE'S GOING
TO PRETTY BIG BY THEN

499
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:09,476
AND SHE'LL NEED SOMEONE
TO HELP HER TIE HER SHOES.

500
00:21:11,062 --> 00:21:12,312
DRIVE HER
TO THE HOSPITAL

501
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:14,899
IN CASE SHE GOES
INTO LABOR...

502
00:21:14,941 --> 00:21:17,651
YOU DON'T HAVE A CAR,
AND YOUR LICENSE EXPIRED.

503
00:21:17,693 --> 00:21:19,195
I KNOW.

504
00:21:19,237 --> 00:21:21,530
YEAH, SEE, THERE'S
SO MUCH TO DO

505
00:21:21,572 --> 00:21:23,616
AND I HAVE SO LITTLE
TIME TO DO IT IN.

506
00:21:30,081 --> 00:21:31,457
ALL RIGHT, CHECK IT OUT.
CHECK THIS OUT.

507
00:21:31,498 --> 00:21:32,792
SAYS HERE
THERE'S A PLACE YOU CAN GO

508
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:35,253
TO RENT VIDEOS
OF ALL THE MUSEUMS.

509
00:21:35,293 --> 00:21:38,131
"IT'S ALMOST
AS GOOD AS BEING THERE."

510
00:21:38,172 --> 00:21:39,673
IT'S BETTER.

511
00:21:39,715 --> 00:21:41,550
YOU CAN'T GO TO A MUSEUM
IN YOUR UNDERWEAR.

512
00:21:43,343 --> 00:21:47,265
WELL, YOU COULD,
BUT PROBABLY JUST THE ONE TIME.

513
00:21:47,306 --> 00:21:49,809
I BET WE COULD
GET VIDEOS OF
ALL THE SIGHTS.

514
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:51,393
GET A VCR IN A HOTEL ROOM

515
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:53,604
WE'D NEVER EVEN HAVE
TO GO OUTSIDE.

516
00:21:53,646 --> 00:21:56,274
IF WE DO THAT,
WE'VE GOT TO RENT DIE HARD.

517
00:21:57,900 --> 00:22:01,154
OH-HO, I BET
THE BRITISH VERSION IS GOOD.

